From: Aveline Noir <jm5905938@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:51:45 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] mm/damon/sysfs: skip registration if DAMON core init fails

DAMON sysfs registers its interface even if DAMON core initialization
fails.  If damon_init() fails to allocate damon_region_cache, starting a
kdamond with an initial region can pass a NULL cache to
kmem_cache_alloc() via damon_new_region().  As a result, NULL
dereference can happen.  The initialization failure is unlikely, but the
consequence is quite bad.

Check damon_initialized() before creating the DAMON sysfs directory and
return -ENOMEM if the core is unavailable.

